## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without confidence"** — every production method is invoked (→ 95% coverage) but almost nothing is actually verified.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests that prove nothing

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | What can break undetected |
|---|------|-------------|--------------------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17-21) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion at all | `Save()` could silently no-op; duplicates never caught |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L31-35) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Price could remain unchanged; wrong product could be updated |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L37-42) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Product could still exist after "delete" |
| 4 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L67-74) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Discount could be applied incorrectly (e.g. `* fraction` instead of `* (1 - fraction)`) |
| 5 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L84-88) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assertion | Parsing errors, wrong field mapping, decimal culture issues all invisible |
| 6 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L62-66) | **Dead variable** — result never asserted | Could return -1 and test still passes |

### 🟠 High — Assertions that are too weak

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Fix needed |
|---|------|-------------|-----------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L25-29) | **Assert.IsNotNull only** — doesn't verify returned data matches | Could return wrong product (different SKU/name/price) |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L45-52) | **Assert.IsNotNull on collection** — doesn't verify count or content | Could return empty list, wrong items, or both products |
| 9 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L55-60) | **Assert.IsNotNull on collection** — doesn't verify count | Could return 0 or 100 items |
| 10 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L76-82) | **Assert.IsNotNull on string** — doesn't verify format | CSV could have wrong delimiters, missing fields, wrong order |

### 🟡 Medium — Structural issues

| # | Issue | Impact |
|---|-------|--------|
| 11 | **No negative-path tests** — `UpdatePrice` on missing SKU should throw `KeyNotFoundException` | Exception behavior untested; could regress to null-ref or silent failure |
| 12 | **No edge-case tests** — empty CSV, negative prices, null SKU, multi-line CSV | Production crashes on malformed input are invisible |
| 13 | **Concrete dependency (`InMemoryStore`) used everywhere** — no mock/fake isolation | Can't verify interaction (e.g. that `Save` is called with correct arguments) |

---

### Concrete Fixes

```csharp
// 1. AddProduct — verify round-trip
[TestMethod]
